UID:95c09ccbeaae60335a6d0b3422e4@global-arts-culture
CATEGORIES:Arts & Culture\,Multidisciplinary\,Madrid\,Spain
DESCRIPTION:Andalusia\, 1937. The Carranza column—composed of horsemen\,
  bullfighters\, Falangists\, landowners\, and Civil Guards—advances thro
 ugh the northern mountains of Seville\, subjugating everything in its path
  and drenching the land in blood\, like Death riding across the fields. A 
 group of women—wives\, mothers\, and neighbors of fugitives and the pers
 ecuted—initiate themselves in the dark language as a form of resistance
 \, forming a coven with the goal of bringing life back to an infertile cou
 ntry with the help of their dead and ghosts. Cosamala is a witch story tha
 t stems from a real Civil War crime and feeds on elements of horror and fo
 lklore to build its own female mythology of vengeance\, love\, and \nCateg
 ory: Multidisciplinary\nOriginal listing: https://www.mataderomadrid.org/e
 n/schedule/presentation-cosamala-alana-s-portero
LOCATION:Casa del Lector\, Plaza de Legazpi\, 8\, Madrid\, 28045
STATUS:CONFIRMED
